          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழலை — maḻalai — \"a toddler; baby talk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "குழந்தையின் மழலைப் பேச்சு எல்லோருக்கும் பிடித்தது. kuḻantaiyiṉ maḻalaip pēccu ellōrukkum piṭittatu. Everyone loved the baby’s first words."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழலைப் பேச்சு, a baby’s talk; மழலையர் பள்ளி, a nursery school."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழலை (maḻalai) is native Dravidian (DEDR 4747), where it means childhood and tender age; the sense of a small child's talk is the everyday one now."
            }
          ]
        },
